\section{Testing phase} \label{testing_results}
Using forecasts made every four weeks during the testing phase, we plot 1- to 28-day ahead incident hospitalization point and 95\% interval forecasts for the eight models of interest during this period in Figures \ref{fig:figure_forecasts_plot_1}. This group consists of six models from the best subset and two Forecast Hub comparison models, the COVIDhub-baseline and the COVIDhub-4\_week\_ensemble. Generally, the THieF ensembles, the original THieF models with 6-week top aggregation levels, and COVIDHub-4\_week\_ensemble appear to better follow the true confirmed hospitalizations compared to the other three models, and these five models also tend to have narrower 95\% interval forecasts. These results are mirrored (and perhaps further explained) by the following stratified evaluations.498

